  "method": "Original embedded A2 pixels only, complete word contexts and selected exact resh/control views. Seven WIS word frames were freshly replayed from the PDF; only5:21 and6:4 received new exact-letter enlargements. The same-page155 resh in הרודים has a naturally enlarged lower foot, so a single lower bulb is insufficient to certify hiriq. The five other WIS positions remain unsupported by the word-level frames and are not claimed to have a newly isolated point. Two S3Y sites received complete glyph views, full source row context and same-page pointed/plain resh comparisons; an independent peer also could not exclude ordinary resh foot plus one point from apparent two-node sheva. Connectedness alone is not a rejection; these shapes fail to distinguish the exact point reliably. No OCR, expected Hebrew, grammatical completion, smoothing or reconstruction supplies a mark.",
